WEBVTT

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.420
The Thanksgiving Day parade is always such great fun.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.820
Look at that Superman balloon!

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:17.920
Don't you just love it?

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.700
I love his music.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.490
Look at those funny-looking clowns.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:39.540
It's for kids.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:48.320
Remember when you and your dad and I

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.540
went to the Thanksgiving Day parade?

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.760
You were four or five years old, I think.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.900
Hello, hello.... Oh, hi, Susan.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:06.780
How are you?... Here's Mom.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:10.680
Hello, Susan.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.120
Yes, he missed a phone call from Alexandra.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.630
Good. Then you'll be here about five?

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:21.680
Oh, fine.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:25.040
I look forward to seeing you and Harry and Michelle.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.320
Drive carefully.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.870
Taste Ellen's turkey dressing.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:32.640
It's delicious.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:34.780
I'm not surprised.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.360
It's Grandma's recipe.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.260
It's my favorite part of the meal.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.280
What about my famous apple pie?

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.840
Dad, your apple pie is my favorite dessert.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:45.520
How's the parade?

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.680
Mom! Is it for me?

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.030
No, Robbie.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.500
Who was it?

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.100
Wrong number.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.060
Philip, would you join me in the kitchen, please?

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:07.780
It's getting late.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.160
We have vegetables to prepare.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.620
Can I help with anything?

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.330
No, honey.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.640
You just relax with Grandpa.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.340
I'll get you to help serve later.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.910
Ellen reminds me so much of Grandma.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.960
What time does the Michigan football game come on?

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:21.620
Four.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.960
I'll be back to see the game.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.320
Grandpa, when did Dad graduate from Michigan?

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.340
Let me think.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.280
He graduated from medical school in 1960

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.600
and from the University of Michigan in 1956.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:43.320
Did you go to Michigan, too, Grandpa?

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:46.300
Yup. I graduated in 1937.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.680
I've got to start thinking about college soon.
